      "body": "\ud83e\udd16 Adding the user-facing cost, from #2485: the tutorial lessons *want* Grout, because a student fills a gap by typing into it. Since a hole as a container's only element is dropped on reload, `14-list-literals.hzt` is forced to spell it `?` instead \u2014 an explicit hole tile, which the student has to select and replace rather than type into. So this bug is not only a persistence asymmetry; it costs the intended editing experience wherever a lesson wants a single blank inside a list or tuple, and the workaround has to be reverted per-lesson once it is fixed.",
